为了配合我那精炼的总结。

156
00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:51.610
And I guess business school was Greg's idea.
我猜上商学院是格雷格的主意。

157
00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:57.290
He always knew at some point down the road he wanted to go to Ryan's business school,
他一直知道以后某个时候他想去瑞安的商学院，

158
00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:59.570
and I guess that card had been on the wall for a while.
我想那张卡片已经在墙上贴了一段时间了。

159
00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:05.990
Well, Angela, speaking of bat storylines, fast fact number one, Joss Whedon directed this episode.
安吉拉，说到蝙蝠的故事线，趣味小常识第一条，乔斯·韦登执导了这一集。

160
00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:13.770
So Joss is famous for creating Buffy the Vampire Slayer, the series starring Sarah Michelle Gellar.
所以乔斯以创作《吸血鬼猎人巴菲》而闻名，这部剧由莎拉·米歇尔·盖拉主演。

161
00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:19.510
This was a huge hit on the WB network, which was run at the time by Suzanne Daniels.
这是WB电视网的巨大热门，当时由苏珊·丹尼尔斯负责管理。

162
00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:23.270
Suzanne's husband is Greg Daniels.
苏珊的丈夫是格雷格·丹尼尔斯。

163
00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:28.530
And that is how Joss kind of got his in to direct an episode of the show.
这就是乔斯得以执导本剧某一集的方式。

164
00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:38.390
But I guess it is just a pure coincidence that he got assigned the episode with a bat and a vampire storyline.
但我猜他被分配到有蝙蝠和吸血鬼故事线的那一集纯属巧合。

165
00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:42.190
I remember he was like, come on, guys, you gave me the bat vampire story.
我记得他当时说，拜托，伙计们，你们把蝙蝠吸血鬼的故事交给了我。

166
00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.630
And we're like, and everyone was like, it is pure coincidence.
然后我们说，每个人都说，这纯属巧合。

167
00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.670
Well, guys, we reached out to writer Brent Forrester.
好了，伙计们，我们联系了编剧布伦特·福斯特。

168
00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:52.270
Remember, he sent in so many amazing audio clips for our grief counseling episode.
还记得吗，他为我们的哀伤辅导那一集发送了那么多精彩的音频片段。

169
00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.190
He did it again this week.
这周他又这么做了。

170
00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:56.590
And here's what he had to say about this.
以下是他对此事的看法。

171
00:07:56.590 --> 00:08:05.030
This episode was directed by Joss Whedon, who was a big, successful television creator at the time and happened to be a big fan of The Office.
这一集由乔斯·韦登执导，他当时是一位大牌、成功的电视制作人，碰巧也是《办公室》的超级粉丝。

172
00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.970
And he approached us asking if he could direct an episode.
他主动找到我们，问他是否可以导演一集。

173
00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:09.350
He ended up directing two.
他最后导演了两集。

174
00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:11.410
And this was the first one that he did.
这是他拍的第一集。

175
00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:19.690
And it's just a total coincidence that the first episode that he directed happens to have a vampire subplot in it.
他导演的第一集恰好有一个吸血鬼的副线剧情，这完全是个巧合。

176
00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:22.330
And he was the creator of Buffy the Vampire Slayer.
而他正是《吸血鬼猎人巴菲》的创作者。

177
00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:31.590
What you notice in that vampire subplot that I remember most is this visual detail that Joss added that was not in the script.
你在那个吸血鬼副线剧情中注意到、我印象最深的是乔斯加入的一个剧本中没有的视觉细节。

178
00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:38.790
If you notice, at the end of the Jim Dwight vampire subplot, Jim says goodbye and leaves the office at the end of the day.
如果你注意到了，在吉姆和德怀特吸血鬼副线剧情的结尾，吉姆在一天结束时说再见并离开了办公室。

179
00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:44.610
And when he does, he turns and he flips up his collar and sort of looks over his shoulder.
当他这么做时，他转身竖起领子，有点像在看他的肩膀后面。

180
00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:50.150
And it's the perfect image of Dracula looking over the corner of his cape.
这简直是德古拉从斗篷角落看出去的完美画面。

181
00:08:50.450 --> 00:09:01.570
And it just works wonderfully as a visual gag, not in the script, totally the contribution of a guy who has worked a long time in the vampire genre.
作为一个视觉笑话，它效果好极了，剧本里没有，完全是一个在吸血鬼题材领域工作了很久的人的贡献。

182
00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:03.110
That was pure Joss Whedon.
那纯粹是乔斯·韦登的风格。

183
00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:04.930
I did not know that.
我不知道这件事。

184
00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:05.850
I didn't know it either.
我也不知道。

185
00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:14.830
And you remember at this time, because I asked Kent Zabornak about this as well, he said that after season two, after we won the Emmy,
你还记得这时候，因为我也向肯·扎博纳克问过这事，他说在第二季之后，在我们赢得艾美奖之后，

186
00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:19.230
we had a bunch of directors reaching out about directing our show.
有一堆导演联系我们想要导演我们的剧。

187
00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.110
Remember, like, Harold Ramis, J.J.
还记得吗，比如哈罗德·雷米斯、J.J.

188
00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:22.910
Abrams?
艾布拉姆斯？

189
00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:24.130
Jason Reitman?
杰森·雷特曼？

190
00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:24.910
Yes.
是的。

191
00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:26.270
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

192
00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:31.170
And Kent would just assign scripts according to director availability.
而肯就会根据导演的档期来分配剧本。

193
00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:35.550
And that is, he confirms, how Joss got this episode.
他证实，这就是乔斯拿到这一集的方式。

194
00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:41.130
So now, fast fact number two, location breakdown with Kentopedia.
那么现在，趣味小常识第二条，肯托百科的外景解析。

195
00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:42.330
Ooh.
噢。

196
00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:46.090
We need a jingle for location breakdown with Kentopedia.
我们需要为肯托百科的外景解析做一个小卡农曲。

197
00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:50.310
Location breakdown with Kentopedia.
肯托百科的外景解析。

198
00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:52.190
Do you like it?
你喜欢吗？

199
00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:52.770
It's okay.
还可以。

200
00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:54.850
I was trying to do, like, a schoolhouse rock thing.
我刚才试图模仿校园摇滚（Schoolhouse Rock）的那种感觉。

201
00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.370
Yeah, I like it.
对，我喜欢。

202
00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:57.030
Okay.
好的。

203
00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:59.250
Okay, location breakdown with Kentopedia.
好的，肯托百科的外景大揭秘。

204
00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.670
Is this about Northridge?
这是关于诺思里奇的吗？

205
00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:01.430
Yes!
没错！

206
00:10:01.770 --> 00:10:03.350
We had a fan question.
我们收到了一个粉丝提问。

207
00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:03.730
B.
B。

208
00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:09.730
Smith, Major Tarwater, Julia Lee, Megan Meeker, Rose Cosette, and Tess Schmidt.
史密斯、塔尔沃特少校、朱莉娅·李、梅根·米克尔、露丝·科赛特和苔丝·施密特。

209
00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:13.290
Where were the business school scenes shot in real life?
商学院的戏份现实中是在哪里拍摄的？

210
00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:15.250
Was it a real classroom on a campus?
那是校园里的真实教室吗？

211
00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:18.130
Were those real students, or were they actors?
那些是真正的学生，还是演员？

212
00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:26.650
Well, as Angela said, Ryan's business school and the scenes with Pam's art school were all shot at Cal State Northridge.
嗯，正如安吉拉所说，瑞恩的商学院以及潘的艺术学校的场景，全都是在加州大学诺思里奇分校拍摄的。

213
00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:28.890
How did you know it was Cal State Northridge, Ange?
安吉，你怎么知道那是加州大学诺思里奇分校的？

214
00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:30.870
Because I listened to the DVD commentary.
因为我听了DVD评论音轨。

215
00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:31.650
Oh!
噢！

216
00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:32.190
Yes!
没错！

217
00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:36.770
Well, Kent said all of the students in the classroom were hired extras,
嗯，肯说教室里的所有学生都是请来的群众演员，

218
00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:44.730
that we used a total of 122 background actors that day for the classroom scenes and the exterior campus scenes.
那天为了教室和校园外景的戏份，我们总共用了122名背景演员。

219
00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:55.610
He said that the business school and the exterior scenes were filmed on day one, and on day two, we filmed the scenes for Pam's art show,
他说商学院和外景是在第一天拍摄的，第二天我们拍摄了潘的艺术展的戏份，

220
00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:59.150
which was held in the Cal State Northridge Design Center.
艺术展是在加州大学诺思里奇分校设计中心举办的。

221
00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:08.310
One of the things I liked that they talked about in the DVD commentary was Brent said they asked all the people playing students if they would please bring their own personal laptop.
他们俩在DVD评论音轨里谈到的一点我很喜欢，布伦特说他们让所有扮演学生的群演都带上自己的个人笔记本电脑。

222
00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:08.910
Oh!
噢！

223
00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:13.650
And when I watched the scene, Jenna, I noticed that all the laptops were different.
珍娜，我看这场戏的时候，注意到所有的笔记本电脑都不一样。

224
00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.210
That is such a good detail.
这细节真的太棒了。

225
00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:16.450
All right.
好吧。

226
00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:17.690
Fast fact number three.
冷知识之三。

227
00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:18.030
Yeah.
对。

228
00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:24.390
Nine days after this episode aired, Rainn Wilson hosted Saturday Night Live.
这集播出九天后，雷恩·威尔逊主持了《周六夜现场》。

229
00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:25.010
Oh, yes!
噢，对！

230
00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:25.770
Do you remember this?
你还记得吗？

231
00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:26.150
Yes!
记得！

232
00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:28.170
We were so excited for him.
我们当时为他感到特别激动。

233
00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:36.590
So we had to kind of move around our shooting schedule to make this happen for Rainn, and I just remember we were all so excited for him.
所以为了迁就雷恩，我们得调整拍摄日程，我只记得我们当时都替他特别兴奋。

234
00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:44.150
And during his opening monologue, he did this bit, it's so funny, where he says, oh,
在他开场独白的时候，他搞了个环节，超级搞笑，他说，噢，

235
00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:49.150
he's just so excited to be at Saturday Night Live because it's just way more exciting than shooting The Office,
他太高兴能来主持《周六夜现场》了，因为这比拍《办公室》刺激多了，

236
00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:53.230
which is basically just sitting at a desk under fluorescent lights all day.
《办公室》基本上就是整天坐在荧光灯下的桌子旁。

237
00:11:53.230 --> 00:12:00.750
He was like, on the set of SNL, there's like scaffolding and there's props and there's costumes and wigs, you know, it feels like a real show.
他说，在SNL片场，有脚手架，有道具，有戏服和假发，你懂的，感觉像个真正的节目。

238
00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:03.410
And he's like, let me show you, let me show you.
然后他说，我带你们看看，我带你们看看。

239
00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:07.730
And he takes the audience on like this backstage tour to show how exciting it is,
接着他带着观众进行了一场后台参观，展示这里有多激动人心，

240
00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:16.790
only to find the cast of Saturday Night Live kind of dressed up doing impersonations of all of our characters from The Office.
结果发现《周六夜现场》的演员们盛装打扮，正在模仿我们《办公室》里的所有角色。

241
00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:20.250
Yes, well, Kristen Wiig is Pam, and she's answering phones.
对，克里斯汀·韦格演的是潘，她在接电话。

242
00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:23.610
Yes, and he's like, hey, Kristen.
对，然后他说，嘿，克里斯汀。

243
00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:27.950
And she's like, SNL, hi, can I help you?
她说，SNL，你好，有什么需要我帮忙的吗？

244
00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:30.250
She's like, I'm just answering phones.
她说，我只是在接电话。

245
00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:31.450
And he's like, what are you doing?
然后他说，你在干什么？

246
00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:32.790
She's like, I do this all the time.
她说，我一直都这样。

247
00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:34.250
I do a lot of things.
我做很多事情呢。

248
00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.670
He's like, don't you do anything else?
他说，你难道不干别的吗？

249
00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.410
And she's like, well, I also like to paint.
然后她说，嗯，我还喜欢画画。

250
00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:42.990
And then she holds up a watercolor painting of 30 Rockefeller Center.
接着她举起了一幅洛克菲勒中心30号的水彩画。

251
00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.590
That's where they film SNL.
那就是他们拍摄《周六夜现场》的地方。

252
00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:53.550
And that is a callback to this episode that had just aired of Pam's watercolor of Dunder Mifflin.
那是对刚刚播出的那一集的一个彩蛋，那一集里有帕姆画的邓德米弗林水彩画。

253
00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:58.050
And I was freaking out excited when I saw it.
我当时看到的时候激动得不得了。

254
00:12:58.270 --> 00:12:59.730
Amy Poehler played me.
艾米·波勒演了我。

255
00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:00.790
Oh, it's so funny.
哦，太搞笑了。

256
00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:05.570
And like had this like sort of like snarl and like kind of flirted with Rain as Dwight.
而且当时她带着那种类似狞笑的表情，还调戏了饰演德怀特的雷恩。

257
00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:11.390
And if you remember, Jenna, Rashida was there that weekend and she's friends with a lot of the SNL cast members.
珍娜，如果你还记得的话，拉什达那个周末也在那儿，她和许多《周六夜现场》的演员都是朋友。

258
00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.370
So they were like, just hop in as Karen.
所以他们就说，直接进来客串卡伦吧。

259
00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:14.850
So she did.
于是她就去了。

260
00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:16.330
He walks down the hall.
他走过走廊。

261
00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:16.630
Yeah.
是啊。

262
00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.790
And they took all these pictures and Rashida emailed them to me.
然后他们拍了所有这些照片，拉什达把它们发邮件给我了。

263
00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:22.230
She was like, Ange, look, it's Amy as you.
她说，安吉，你看，这是演你的艾米。

264
00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:26.330
And I have all of these great pictures of them from the set that day.
我留着所有他们那天在片场的精彩照片。

265
00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:27.450
Amazing.
太棒了。

266
00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:28.750
Are you going to put those on the pod?
你要把这些发到播客上吗？

267
00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:29.930
On Office League's pod?
发到 Office League 的播客上吗？

268
00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:30.790
Yes, I'll put one.
对，我会发一张。

269
00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:31.810
I have a great one.
我有一张很棒的照片。

270
00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.790
I think I have a group shot I'll put on the pod.
我想我有一张合影会发到播客上。

271
00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:37.570
Well, listen to what Kristen Wiig did after that episode aired.
好吧，听听克里斯汀·韦格在那一集播出后做了什么。

272
00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:37.990
What?
什么？

273
00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:41.130
So she and I shared a manager and we'd met a few times.
所以她和我共用一个经纪人，我们见过好几次面。

274
00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:44.970
We were both really struggling actresses at the same time.
我们当时都是在同一时期苦苦挣扎的女演员。

275
00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:48.210
And kind of when I got on The Office, she got on Saturday Night Live.
差不多就在我加入《办公室》的时候，她加入了《周六夜现场》。

276
00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:49.830
So this was really thrilling to us.
所以这让我们感到非常激动。

277
00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:51.390
I get a package in the mail.
我收到了一件邮寄的包裹。

278
00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.490
It is the watercolor.
就是那幅水彩画。

279
00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:54.690
Oh, come on.
哦，拜托。

280
00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:56.250
That she held up on the show.
她在节目中举的那幅画。

281
00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:58.090
She signed the back of it.
她在背面签了名。

282
00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:03.250
And then she wrote me the nicest note that was just like, I just know what it would mean
然后她给我写了一张非常贴心的便条，大意是，我很清楚如果有一天我在这个电视节目里被恶搞

283
00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:08.750
to me if I were ever parodied on this television show.
对我来说意味着什么。

284
00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.730
And I thought you might like to have a prop from the moment.
我想你可能会想要那个时刻的一个道具。

285
00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:14.250
So I asked if I could send this to you.
所以我问我能不能把它寄给你。

286
00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:15.250
And they said yes.
他们同意了。

287
00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:16.730
That is so lovely.
这太惹人喜爱了。

288
00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:17.490
Yeah.
是啊。

289
00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:20.470
And I have it framed and it's in my family room.
我把它装裱起来挂在我的家庭活动室里。

290
