接着迈克尔到达了校园。

449
00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:14.840
He is so excited.
他太兴奋了。

450
00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:20.780
There's just all of these memories coming back to him that he's having that might have occurred
所有的这些回忆都涌上了他的心头，那些可能曾经发生过的

451
00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:22.600
if he had ever attended college.
如果他曾经上过大学的话。

452
00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.720
That made me sad, by the way.
顺便说一句，这让我很难过。

453
00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:26.560
It made me sad, too.
我也觉得很难过。

454
00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:28.460
I mean, Michael would have loved college.
我是说，迈克尔一定会很喜欢大学的。

455
00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:32.100
I think Michael would have been like an RA in the dorm, you know?
我觉得迈克尔在宿舍里会像个宿管助理（RA）一样，你知道吗？

456
00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:33.000
100%.
百分之百。

457
00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:35.400
And he probably would have been like a lifer RA.
而且他大概会当一辈子的宿管助理。

458
00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.200
They probably would have been like, you can leave now.
他们大概会说，你现在可以走了。

459
00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:39.600
And he's like, no, we got another batch of students coming in.
而他会说，不，我们还有新的一批学生要来。

460
00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:41.280
And they're like, you're not a student anymore.
然后他们会说，你已经不是学生了。

461
00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:42.480
Yeah.
是啊。

462
00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:43.620
Yeah.
对。

463
00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:44.260
That's true.
确实如此。

464
00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:46.200
It's true.
没错。

465
00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:50.340
Well, we had a fan comment from Amber Morris.
嗯，我们收到了一个来自安布尔·莫里斯的粉丝评论。

466
00:21:50.520 --> 00:21:50.680
Okay.
好的。

467
00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:56.080
You know that moment when Michael runs up and tries to join the Frisbee game?
你知道迈克尔跑过去试图加入飞盘比赛那个时刻吗？

468
00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:56.440
Yeah.
记得。

469
00:21:56.660 --> 00:21:59.140
She says, fun fast fact.
她说，一个有趣的冷知识。

470
00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:04.360
A friend of mine, Nathan Blank, played the Frisbee student at Ryan's school.
我的一个朋友内森·布兰克，在瑞安的学校里扮演那个玩飞盘的学生。

471
00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:07.640
Michael ran up and stole a Frisbee and threw it.
迈克尔跑过来抢走了一个飞盘并把它扔了出去。

472
00:22:07.820 --> 00:22:10.300
And Nathan's line was something like, dude.
内森的台词大概是，老兄。

473
00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:16.640
And he has had nothing but wonderful things to say about his filming day and working with Steve and BJ.
对于当天的拍摄以及和史蒂夫还有B.J.合作，他赞不绝口，全都是美好的回忆。

474
00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.660
Aw, I love that.
噢，我真喜欢这个。

475
00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:20.660
But yeah, that is very sweet.
不过是的，这真的很温馨。

476
00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:26.040
That scene made me laugh really hard because everything about how Steve approached that Frisbee was wrong.
那场戏让我笑得前仰后合，因为史蒂夫对待那个飞盘的方式从头到尾都是错的。

477
00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:29.520
No one should ever grab a Frisbee and throw it that way.
任何人都不应该那样去抓飞盘并把它扔出去。

478
00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:31.860
And it just was so perfect.
而且真的是太完美了。

479
00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:36.120
Well, now we're going to go back to the office, Angela.
好了，安吉拉，现在我们要回到办公室了。

480
00:22:36.640 --> 00:22:43.760
Because now that other card that Brent talked about, the one that says bad in office, is about to go into play.
因为既然布伦特谈到的那张卡片——写着办公室里的坏事的那个——马上就要派上用场了。

481
00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:44.960
We're in the office.
我们回到了办公室。

482
00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:47.820
Dwight sees some kind of animal feces.
德怀特发现了一些某种动物的粪便。

483
00:22:48.780 --> 00:22:50.020
He's on the case.
他开始着手调查了。

484
00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:53.840
He's like, oh, there's a bird in the rafters, guys.
他说，哦，天呐，屋梁上有只鸟，伙计们。

485
00:22:54.460 --> 00:22:55.580
But it's not a bird.
但那不是鸟。

486
00:22:55.680 --> 00:22:56.360
It's a bat.
是只蝙蝠。

487
00:22:56.400 --> 00:22:56.560
No.
不。

488
00:22:56.680 --> 00:22:58.500
And everyone freaks out.
然后所有人都吓疯了。

489
00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:01.160
Everyone except Jim and Creed.
除了吉姆和克里德，所有人。

490
00:23:01.460 --> 00:23:01.840
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

491
00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:02.580
Creed is ready.
克里德已经准备好了。

492
00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:05.700
Angela stops, drops, and rolls.
安吉拉就地卧倒并翻滚。

493
00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:06.060
Yeah.
没错。

494
00:23:06.520 --> 00:23:07.560
Stanley leaves.
斯坦利直接走了。

495
00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:12.600
Eventually, Dwight is able to lock the bat in the conference room after a bunch of mayhem.
最终，在经历了一阵混乱之后，德怀特设法把蝙蝠锁在了会议室里。

496
00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:18.600
Fan question from Leona Woldridge, Ruth Rodriguez, Heather Flynn, and Abby Moll.
来自莱昂娜·沃尔德里奇、露丝·罗德里格斯、希瑟·弗林和艾比·莫尔的粉丝提问。

497
00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:23.520
At approximately five minutes, Angela drops and rolls while the bat flies around.
在大约五分钟的时候，在蝙蝠四处飞舞时，安吉拉就地卧倒并翻滚。

498
00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:29.160
Then you barely hear her voice in the background, either talking to herself or praying.
然后你可以隐约听到她在背景里发出声音，要么是在自言自语，要么是在祈祷。

499
00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:30.160
Do you know what you're saying?
你知道你当时在说什么吗？

500
00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:30.520
I do.
我知道。

501
00:23:30.780 --> 00:23:35.000
I remember Joss saying to me, all right, Angela would totally freak out.
我记得乔斯跟我说，好吧，安吉拉肯定会吓坏的。

502
00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:37.780
And we talked about, what did that look like?
然后我们讨论过，那会是什么样的情景？

503
00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:40.440
And would I drop to the ground?
我会直接倒地吗？

504
00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:44.060
And I came up with this dropping to the ground and rolling.
然后我想出了倒地并翻滚这个动作。

505
00:23:44.780 --> 00:23:45.860
That's my memory, Jenna.
詹娜，这是我的记忆。

506
00:23:46.380 --> 00:23:48.780
That I dropped to the ground and I decided to roll.
我倒在了地上，然后决定翻滚。

507
00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:50.680
And Joss really liked that.
乔斯真的很喜欢这样。

508
00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:54.640
And then I just laid face down on the carpet and I improvised this.
然后我就脸朝下趴在毛毯上，即兴发挥了这一段。

509
00:23:54.760 --> 00:23:57.980
And I said something like, God, this is Angela Martin.
我说了一些类似的话，天哪，我是安吉拉·马丁。

510
00:23:58.860 --> 00:24:01.640
Please don't let that stupid thing come anywhere near me.
请千万别让那该死的东西靠近我半步。

511
00:24:01.860 --> 00:24:03.740
And I just sort of mumbled these prayers.
然后我就嘟囔着这些祈祷的话。

512
00:24:04.020 --> 00:24:04.840
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

513
00:24:04.980 --> 00:24:11.840
When I was a child and I would pray, I would lead with, God, this is Jenna Fisher.
当我还是个孩子的时候，每次祈祷，我都会以“天哪，我是詹娜·费舍尔”开头。

514
00:24:12.480 --> 00:24:14.320
I would lead with an introduction.
我会用自我介绍来开场。

515
00:24:14.920 --> 00:24:15.400
Same.
我也是。

516
00:24:16.240 --> 00:24:16.720
100%.
百分之百。

517
00:24:16.720 --> 00:24:16.940
Yeah.
对。

518
00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:19.720
I was like, well, I need God to know.
当时我想，好吧，我得让上帝知道。

519
00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:22.900
Like, I need him to like key in to who are these prayers for?
就像是，我需要他弄清楚这些祈祷是为谁准备的？

520
00:24:23.260 --> 00:24:26.820
As I'm receiving these prayers, who are they coming from?
当我收到这些祈祷时，它们是从哪儿来的？

521
00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:28.740
So I thought, well, I'll lead with my name.
所以我认为，好吧，我得报上我的名字。

522
00:24:28.960 --> 00:24:31.800
I used to say, Lord God, this is Angela Kinsey.
我以前总是说，主啊，我是安吉拉·金西。

523
00:24:32.100 --> 00:24:33.000
I'm in my bedroom.
我在我的卧室里。

524
00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:37.780
I am on a street called Kavling in Jakarta, Indonesia.
我在印度尼西亚雅加达一条叫卡夫林的长街上。

525
00:24:38.420 --> 00:24:40.360
That is in the Southern Hemisphere.
那里在南半球。

526
00:24:41.320 --> 00:24:42.600
It's a group of islands.
那是一个群岛。

527
00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:44.560
I'm just below the equator.
我就在赤道下方。

528
00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:46.260
I would do this.
我以前就这样做过。

529
00:24:46.640 --> 00:24:49.320
Like, I needed him to know where I was.
就像，我需要他知道我在哪里。

530
00:24:49.720 --> 00:24:52.640
That was some serious location honing right there.
那可真是精确锁定地理位置了。

531
00:24:52.860 --> 00:24:57.300
You were like, the coordinates are 75 degrees latitude.
你当时就像是在说，坐标是北纬75度。

532
00:24:59.060 --> 00:25:00.060
I'm in my bedroom.
我在我的卧室里。

533
00:25:00.100 --> 00:25:01.520
It's down the hall on the right.
它在走廊尽头的右边。

534
00:25:01.520 --> 00:25:04.320
It's across from the bathroom.
正对着浴室。

535
00:25:04.820 --> 00:25:05.600
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

536
00:25:06.340 --> 00:25:09.920
I did not get that specific, but I applaud that.
我没有具体到这种程度，但我为你点赞。

537
00:25:09.920 --> 00:25:10.240
Thank you.
谢谢你。

538
00:25:10.540 --> 00:25:13.120
Then we had more fan questions about this scene.
接下来我们还有关于这场戏的更多粉丝提问。

539
00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:19.780
From Rosalie W., Tanner W., Mia F., and Jacob W.
来自罗莎莉·W、坦纳·W、米亚·F和雅各布·W。

540
00:25:19.780 --> 00:25:23.480
Was the bat that got trapped in the office a real bat?
困在办公室里的那只蝙蝠是真的蝙蝠吗？

541
00:25:24.020 --> 00:25:30.360
Kentopedia says, yes, we used a real bat for three scenes.
肯托百科说，是的，我们在三个场景中用了一只真蝙蝠。

542
00:25:30.620 --> 00:25:34.980
The scene where Dwight stands on Pam's reception desk to look inside the ceiling.
德怀特站在帕姆的前台桌子上查看天花板内部的那个场景。

543
00:25:35.680 --> 00:25:39.100
A few shots of the bat on the ceiling in the conference room.
会议室天花板上蝙蝠的几个镜头。

544
00:25:39.420 --> 00:25:42.900
And for that shot of the bat on the ceiling in the kitchen.
还有厨房天花板上蝙蝠的那个镜头。

545
00:25:43.320 --> 00:25:48.140
Kent hired two bat wranglers to provide us with the bat, Chad Dunn and John Baldwin.
肯雇了两位蝙蝠驯养师来为我们提供蝙蝠，查德·邓恩和约翰·鲍德温。

546
00:25:48.440 --> 00:25:54.900
And they put Chad up in the ceiling to hold the bat for that scene where Dwight peers in.
他们把查德安排在天花板上，在德怀特往里张望的那场戏里拿着蝙蝠。

547
00:25:55.320 --> 00:25:57.180
The one we were just talking about.
就是我们刚才谈到的那场。

548
00:25:57.180 --> 00:26:01.740
Now, the rest of the time when we see the bat flying around, that was all CGI.
至于剩下的时间里我们看到蝙蝠飞来飞去，那全都是特效。

549
00:26:03.060 --> 00:26:06.740
Kent said he hired Mitch Suskin as our visual effects supervisor.
肯说他雇了米奇·萨斯金担任我们的视觉特效总监。

550
00:26:06.740 --> 00:26:08.880
He was great, did a terrific job.
他很棒，干得非常出色。

551
00:26:09.120 --> 00:26:12.740
And they worked with several production houses to animate the bat.
而且他们与几家制作公司合作来制作蝙蝠的动画。

552
00:26:13.320 --> 00:26:20.260
And then there was a third kind of bat that we used, which we will talk about later in the scene with Kate.
然后我们还用了第三种蝙蝠，我们稍后会在与凯特的戏份中聊到。

553
00:26:20.520 --> 00:26:20.920
Yes.
是的。

554
00:26:21.040 --> 00:26:22.960
And it was a mechanical bat.
那是一只机械蝙蝠。

555
00:26:23.180 --> 00:26:23.420
Yes.
没错。

556
00:26:24.080 --> 00:26:25.320
So three different bats.
所以总共有三种不同的蝙蝠。

557
00:26:25.600 --> 00:26:26.100
Three different bats.
三种不同的蝙蝠。

558
00:26:26.100 --> 00:26:28.080
I have a tiny bit of bat trivia.
我有一点关于蝙蝠的冷知识。

559
00:26:28.420 --> 00:26:29.620
Oh, lay it on me.
哦，说来听听。

560
00:26:29.680 --> 00:26:29.880
Okay.
好的。

561
00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.860
Here's my little bit of bat trivia from this episode.
这是我从本集节目中收集到的一点蝙蝠冷知识。

562
00:26:33.160 --> 00:26:36.860
In the DVD commentary, Rain says he named the bat.
在DVD评论音轨中，雷恩说他给这只蝙蝠取了名字。

563
00:26:37.320 --> 00:26:39.440
That he was talking to the bat wrangler.
当时他在跟蝙蝠驯养员聊天。

564
00:26:39.720 --> 00:26:41.540
And Rain said, what's his name?
雷恩问，它叫什么名字？

565
00:26:41.820 --> 00:26:45.180
And the bat wrangler was like, oh, we've never given him a name.
蝙蝠驯养员说，哦，我们从来没给它起过名字。

566
00:26:45.320 --> 00:26:46.300
And Rain was like, what?
然后雷恩说，什么？

567
00:26:47.220 --> 00:26:48.200
I'm going to name him.
我要给它起个名字。

568
00:26:48.420 --> 00:26:51.200
And so Rain named the bat Gary.
于是雷恩给这只蝙蝠取名叫加里。

569
00:26:51.920 --> 00:26:53.760
It's Gary the bat.
也就是蝙蝠加里。

570
00:26:53.940 --> 00:26:55.420
And we called him Gary all week.
我们那一整周都叫它加里。

571
00:26:56.220 --> 00:26:57.780
Well, good job, Gary.
干得好，加里。

572
00:26:58.080 --> 00:26:58.240
Yeah.
是的。

573
00:26:58.620 --> 00:27:04.220
And now my question is, Rain, if you ever listen to this, is that Michael Gary, Scott?
现在我的问题是，雷恩，如果你哪天听到这个，（这个名字）是来自迈克尔·加里·斯科特吗？

574
00:27:05.720 --> 00:27:06.220
Oh.
哦。

575
00:27:06.700 --> 00:27:07.060
Oh.
哦。

576
00:27:07.940 --> 00:27:09.180
Or is it just Gary?
还是就叫加里？

577
00:27:09.380 --> 00:27:10.320
Just Gary the bat.
就叫蝙蝠加里。

578
00:27:11.340 --> 00:27:22.360
Well, I remember shooting this scene, Angela, because they laid out for us this very elaborate trail of how the bat would fly so that we could all react to it.
安吉拉，我记得拍这场戏的时候，他们为我们规划了一条非常复杂的蝙蝠飞行路线，好让我们所有人都能对它做出反应。

579
00:27:22.440 --> 00:27:23.780
Because we're reacting to nothing.
因为我们当时面对的是空气做出反应。

580
00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:25.980
Nothing is flying through the ceiling.
什么都没有从天花板飞过。

581
00:27:26.240 --> 00:27:26.340
Right.
对的。

582
00:27:26.340 --> 00:27:34.280
And so it was really choreographed, like, bat is here, bat is there, bat swoops here, bat goes into conference room.
所以这真的排练得很细致，比如，蝙蝠在这里，蝙蝠在那里，蝙蝠从这里俯冲，蝙蝠飞进会议室。

583
00:27:35.000 --> 00:27:37.020
And I, it looks so real.
而且，它看起来太真实了。

584
00:27:37.320 --> 00:27:37.500
Yeah.
对啊。

585
00:27:38.560 --> 00:27:42.700
So, yeah, guys, we are screaming at and reacting to nothing flying through the office.
所以，伙计们，我们当时是在对着办公室里空气中飞过的虚无尖叫和反应。

586
00:27:42.720 --> 00:27:44.040
Yeah, we're not freaking out the bat.
对，我们可没有吓唬蝙蝠。

587
00:27:44.240 --> 00:27:45.280
We're not screaming at him.
我们没有对着它尖叫。

588
00:27:46.180 --> 00:27:48.840
I have a few background catches from this scene.
我在这场戏里抓到了一些背景细节。

589
00:27:49.760 --> 00:27:50.940
Lay them on me.
说来听听。

590
00:27:50.940 --> 00:27:54.920
Three minutes, 54 seconds, Pam is sketching a tape dispenser.
3分54秒时，帕姆在素描一个胶带座。

591
00:27:56.360 --> 00:27:56.760
Yeah.
对。

592
00:27:56.920 --> 00:27:58.380
We don't see it, though, at the art show.
不过我们在画展上没看到这个。

593
00:27:59.120 --> 00:28:02.220
Well, she doesn't have time to watercolor that before the art show.
嗯，她在画展之前可没时间画这个水彩画。

594
00:28:02.240 --> 00:28:02.600
Well, I didn't know.
好吧，我不知道嘛。

595
00:28:02.600 --> 00:28:04.360
This is just something she's doing on the side.
这只是她顺手画着玩的。

596
00:28:04.400 --> 00:28:05.280
Well, that's what I was going to ask.
好吧，这正是我要问的。

597
00:28:05.360 --> 00:28:08.260
Is she last minute trying to hustle up some more art for her wall?
她是在临阵磨枪，想为她的墙面多凑几幅画吗？

598
00:28:08.480 --> 00:28:08.840
Okay.
好吧。

599
00:28:08.840 --> 00:28:12.720
No, she just has a light work day and she's sketching at her desk.
